findings.body:
**Claimed critical; verifier found:** verifier off

Any authenticated caller can set `body.accountId` and read that account; nothing verifies support-staff role or that `id === caller.accountId`.

Failure mode: a normal user sends `{"accountId":"<victim>"}`, passes `auth(req)`, and gets the victim row from `db.accounts.findUnique`.

Fix: keep self-lookup as the default path, and only honor an explicit account id after an authorization check (e.g. `caller.isSupport` / role claim). Example:

```suggestion
  const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
  const id: string = body.accountId ?? caller.accountId;
  if (id !== caller.accountId && !caller.isSupport) {
    return Response.json({ error: "forbidden" }, { status: 403 });
  }
  const account = await db.accounts.findUnique({ where: { id } });
```

Adapt `isSupport` to whatever staff signal `auth()` already exposes.
